    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 18,
      "bbox": [
        488,
        168,
        549,
        901
      ],
      "margin_number": 1,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "μείζονα Comparative. See GE pp. 136–138, #154–160 for more forms. Note that there are two ways of saying more … than …: GE pp. 137, #158 and GE p. 164, #180(e).",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 19,
      "bbox": [
        552,
        168,
        609,
        898
      ],
      "margin_number": 4,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "εὐδαιμονεστέραν This is another form of the comparative; see GE p. 166, #182. It is easily recognisable, as is the superlative which follows in the next line.",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 20,
      "bbox": [
        612,
        168,
        653,
        836
      ],
      "margin_number": 9,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "τί παθόντες Aorist participle of πάσχω, second aor. ἔπαθον. Literally ‘having experienced what, and wanting what, are you leaving?’",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 21,
      "bbox": [
        656,
        157,
        671,
        792
      ],
      "margin_number": 13,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "τοιοῦτον τὸ πάθος πάθος is a neuter noun 3c. τοιοῦτον = ‘such’.",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 22,
      "bbox": [
        674,
        123,
        715,
        885
      ],
      "margin_number": 13,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "–14 εἰς τὸ δικαστήριον Note the -ηριον ending which denotes a place where an activity takes place. Cf. φροντιστήριον.",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 23,
      "bbox": [
        718,
        158,
        759,
        831
      ],
      "margin_number": 16,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "κατεψηφίσαντο ψηφίζομαι means ‘I vote’. καταψηφίσομαι means ‘I condemn’, ἀποψηφίζομαι means ‘I acquit’.",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 24,
      "bbox": [
        762,
        158,
        818,
        907
      ],
      "margin_number": 20,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "οἱ μὲν γὰρ τέττιγες … For the Athenian love of litigation see also Section 6B lines 23–24, where Strepsiades cannot believe that it is Athens on the map because there are no jurors sitting.",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 25,
      "bbox": [
        821,
        157,
        835,
        674
      ],
      "margin_number": 30,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "ἀποκρινοῦμαι What is the tense? Cf. ἀποκρίνομαι.",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
